      "writtenOn": "2023-09-15T22:07:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`java_api_contribution` modules are indeed dependencies of `java_api_library`, but they only provide the api files (e.g. `*-current.txt` files), and all of them are being created in the `DroidstubsFactory`. Therefore, `checkCurrentApiTimestamp` is not defined at the phase of creation of `java_api_contribution` modules as they are [initialized during `GenerateAndroidBuildAction` of droidstubs](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/java/droidstubs.go;drc\u003d504d3565790b0dc5220f9c9c7ae230fad758fed7;l\u003d757). Thus I thought that it is infeasible to inject `checkCurrentApiTimestamp` to `java_api_contribution`, and added the phony target as the validation instead. Please let me know if there is a way to do so, and I will make modifications.",
      "parentUuid": "3bbf43f4_c19005a8",
      "revId": "2a757193d82f3a0df6311eedf7d03989e0dcf119",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
